<p>As anomalies go, &quot;beer pox&quot; is kinda just okay, but the amount of depth and story around this is fantastic. I can't believe I never saw the Chicago Spirit before, it's only two years old, but the time period is presented perfectly.</p>
<p>My only criticism would be the slang in the interview &#8212; are they really going to write something like &quot;tryna&quot;? &#8212; and a bit of confusion about the final iteration. It seemed like you were setting up the idea that the Foundation's efforts to eradicate this disease were mutating it, since <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">hydrargyrum</span> mercury shows up at the end of part one and the description of part two. I was expecting silicates in part three, but they never appeared, so it was a little disconcerting. But even as is, totally worth an upvote.</p>

