			<div class="content" id="post-content-2570043">
									

<p>Mimicry is a real thing. Mimicry in macrofauna is also generally &quot;blend in with the background&quot; thing. The reason there are insects that look like sticks but no horses that look like sticks is because insects breed very very fast and there's very very many of them.</p>
<p>This is some sort of bacterium, but I'll classify this as a macrofauna because it's big as fuck and also spreads under very odd and very specific conditions.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>People would probably still drink vaguely coke shaped bottles labeled &quot;Cccc-ooo&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You know, probably not. People will drink store-brand soda, but they will not drink obviously counterfeit shit. Whiskey is an another question</p>

